ccupying the center with a pawn. White's b2-b4 move doesn't contest the center, so I should seize the opportunity to establish a strong central presence. This move:\n- Controls key central squares (d4 and f4)\n- Opens lines for my dark-squared bishop and queen\n- Follows classical opening principles\n- Gives me a slight initiative since White has played a flank move rather than contesting the center\n\nAnswer: P: e7-e5"}
