ost centralized, powerful square available\n- The e4 knight is difficult to dislodge (White's d-pawn hasn't moved)\n- It attacks f2, adding pressure near White's king\n- It removes my knight from potential harassment by the g4 pawn\n- It's an active, developing move that improves my position immediately\n- The centralized knight coordinates well with my advanced e5 pawn\n\nAnswer: N: f6-e4"}
