 to control the long diagonal.\n- **N: b8-d7**: More passive knight development, but prepares to support the center.\n\nReason:\nI choose **N: b8-c6** because:\n1. It develops a piece to its most natural square\n2. The knight on c6 supports my central pawn on d5\n3. It controls important central squares (d4, e5, e7, a5)\n4. It's a flexible move that doesn't commit to a specific pawn structure yet\n5. After this, I can develop my bishops and prepare to castle\n6. Knights are generally best developed before bishops, following opening principles\n\nAnswer: N: b8-c6"}
