the knight on b1 doesn't control d1.\n\nReason: Capturing the rook on d1 wins significant material (approximately 5 points of value) with no immediate compensation for White. This is a clean tactical win that puts me up a full rook, which should be easily winning in the endgame. The move is forcing and concrete.\n\nAnswer: Q: e1-d1"}
