ikely defend.\n\n5. **B: c8-g4** - Developing my bishop with tempo, but doesn't capitalize on the queen's position.\n\nThe most critical factor is that my queen is already deep in enemy territory. I should use this to deliver check and maintain maximum pressure.\n\nReason: Q: d1-f1 delivers check to the White king, forcing White to respond immediately. This maintains the initiative and keeps White on the defensive. After Kh1 (forced), I can continue to harass the king or exploit the weakened position. Giving check is the most forcing move available and doesn't allow White time to consolidate or counterattack.\n\nAnswer: Q: d1-f1"}
