e bishop active on a strong diagonal.\n\n4. **R: f8-d8** or **R: f8-e8** - Centralizing the rook, preparing to potentially double on key files.\n\n5. **B: c8-f5** - Develops the bishop to an active square, controlling key central squares.\n\nReason: **B: c8-g4** is my choice because it:\n- Develops my last minor piece actively\n- Puts immediate pressure on White's position\n- Controls important squares around White's compromised king position\n- Coordinates well with my other pieces for a potential attack\n- The bishop on g4 can create threats and tactical opportunities\n\nAnswer: B: c8-g4"}
