ng to move to a worse square\n- Maintains pressure with my well-coordinated pieces\n- The bishop on d3 will be actively placed for further attacks\n\nReason: B: e2-d3 gives check and forces White's king into an even more precarious position. This check will likely disrupt White's coordination and allow me to consolidate my advantage with my superior piece activity. The king will have to move to e1, e3, g1, g2, or g3, all of which leave it vulnerable to further tactical blows.\n\nAnswer: B: e2-d3"}
