** - Similar to above, supporting the d-pawn.\n\nReason: The passed pawn on d3 is my biggest winning asset. Pushing it to d2 creates an immediate and severe threat of promotion on the next move. White's pieces are not well-coordinated to stop this pawn - the white king on f3 is too far away, and the rook on a1 or knight on b1 would need time to blockade. By pushing d3-d2, I force White into a desperate defensive position, and with my material advantage (extra rook), I should be able to support the pawn's promotion or win material while White tries to stop it.\n\nAnswer: P: d3-d2"}
