ars undefended. The White knight on b1 cannot protect it adequately.\n\nReason: Re1+ is clearly the best move. It gives check to the White king on f3, forcing it to move, and simultaneously attacks the undefended rook on a1. After the king moves to escape check, I can capture the rook with Rxa1, winning White's most valuable remaining piece. This transforms my material advantage into an overwhelming position where checkmating will be straightforward with two rooks and a bishop versus just a knight and pawns.\n\nAnswer: R: e8-e1"}
