nly go to d2 or a3)\n- If the knight moves, I can continue to dominate with my rook\n\nReason: R: e8-e1 is the strongest move because it attacks the undefended knight on b1 while seizing control of White's back rank. The knight has very limited options, and after it moves, my rook will dominate the position. This move maximizes my material advantage and converts it into a winning position.\n\nAnswer: R: e8-e1"}
