omplishes multiple goals:\n- Forces White's King to move to a potentially worse square\n- Activates my Rook aggressively on the second rank\n- Maintains the initiative with tempo\n- In rook and bishop endgames, active piece play and controlling key squares is critical\n- This prepares for potential back-rank threats and coordinated attacks with my bishop\n\nAnswer: R: e1-e2"}
