 maintains maximum pressure and doesn't allow White any counterplay\n\nReason: With such a large material advantage (rook and bishop vs knight), I should play actively and forcefully. Giving check with R: e1-e4+ displaces White's centralized king, gains tempo, and allows me to further coordinate my pieces for a winning attack. This move maintains the initiative and brings me closer to converting my material advantage into a win.\n\nAnswer: R: e1-e4"}
