ority advancement.\n\nReason: B: c5-f2 is the strongest move because:\n- It places the bishop on an active, long diagonal\n- It restricts White's king mobility significantly\n- It prepares to support my pawn advances on the kingside\n- The bishop controls critical central and kingside squares\n- It maintains flexibility for my subsequent plans\n\nAnswer: B: c5-f2"}
