 accomplishes multiple objectives: it attacks the c5 pawn, centralizes my king powerfully, cuts off the White king from supporting its pawns, and prepares to either capture the c5 pawn or blockade White's pawn advances. This move maximizes my winning chances by using my most powerful piece (the king in endgames) actively while maintaining my material advantage.\n\nAnswer: K: e6-d5"}
