d bishop.\n\n**Reason:**\nPushing **a5-a4** is the most forcing move. It advances my furthest passed pawn, and White's pieces cannot adequately blockade it. After a5-a4, the pawn will be on a4, just 3 squares from promotion. White's king on c4 would need to spend moves catching it, but my king can support from d7-c6, and my bishop controls key squares. This creates immediate threats that White must address, making it the most concrete path to victory.\n\n**Answer: P: a5-a4**"}
