one square closer to queening. With my Bishop on d4 already controlling key diagonal squares and my King well-positioned on d6, the c-pawn can advance safely. White's King on b4 cannot stop this pawn from eventually promoting, especially with my pieces providing support. This is the most forcing move that brings me closest to a decisive advantage.\n\nAnswer: P: c4-c3"}
